# cw2 runtime configs. With `num_gpus: auto` cw2 calls _persist_runtime_config
# (cw_slurm.py), which writes a fully-resolved snapshot of the config next to the
# original on every submit: "relative_<config>.yml" plus a per-experiment-name
# directory holding "relative_<config>_<exp name>.yml". That snapshot -- not the
# hand-written YAML -- is what the submitted job actually reads, so it pins the
# GPU-node assignment made at submit time. Regenerated every submit, never edited
# by hand. Ignoring the files also keeps the generated directory untracked, since
# it contains nothing else.
relative_*.yml
